    "summary": "Jam‑focused set with strong Let It Grow and Bird Song",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a solid second‑set jam stretch highlighted by Let It Grow with horn textures and an inspired Weather Report Suite. Bird Song shines in the first set while Eyes Of The World flows smoothly into Stella Blue. Overall energy is medium but the playing remains engaging throughout.",
    "review": "On September 12, 1973 at William and Mary College Hall the Dead rolled out a relaxed yet intriguingly jam‑centric performance. The first set moves through familiar terrain—Bertha, Mexicali Blues and Brown Eyed Women—before Bird Song rises as a standout moment, its lyrical phrasing underscored by Jerry’s crystal‑clear tone. The second set is where the show truly finds its groove: Loose Lucy opens the set with a loose, swinging feel, then Weather Report Suite (Prelude → Part 1) blossoms into a horn‑enhanced Let It Grow that showcases a wild dual‑guitar attack from Jerry and Bob. Eyes Of The World segues seamlessly into Stella Blue, offering a smooth transition that highlights the band's collective breathing. The night rounds out with a spirited Casey Jones and an encore of One More Saturday Night that leaves the crowd smiling. While the soundboard recordings suffer occasional funky or low‑volume quirks, the musical moments stand strong enough to make this a worthwhile listen for fans of the early‑fall ’73 era.",
